# Replace the older first-Airbnb walkthrough's universal financing/timeline claims
# with an actionable purchase file. The hub remains the task directory.
from pillars import sections_html
sections=[
('1. Write a buy box you can fund',[
 'If you are ready to buy your first Airbnb, write down the cash you can allocate, the liquidity you must retain, the markets you will investigate and the owner work you will accept. Specify a price ceiling, property type, guest profile and the evidence that would make you reject a deal. A first purchase should have a written boundary before you open a listing portal.',
 'Use the <a href="/tools/first-str-purchase-budget/">first-STR purchase cash planner</a>. It separates down payment, closing, furnishing, repairs, service fees and retained reserves. Its inputs are planning assumptions, not lender requirements. Keep a separate personal emergency fund outside the cash you allocate to the property.']),
('2. Confirm financing before searching seriously',[
 'Tell the lender the intended investment use and discuss your borrower profile, available funds and property guardrails. Ask what remains conditional, which property types qualify and what cash must remain after closing. A maximum approval amount is one constraint, not the amount you should automatically spend.',
 'The <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/get-a-preapproval-letter/" rel="noopener">CFPB explains that a preapproval is not a guaranteed loan offer</a>. Get the actual address reviewed before relying on that letter for a purchase. Use our <a href="/blog/str-mortgage-preapproval-before-property/">STR preapproval guide</a> to organize lender questions.']),
('3. Find properties for sale that fit the first-property plan',[
 'Search ordinary homes as well as listings advertised as existing Airbnbs. A furnished listing can reduce some setup work but may come with maintenance, association fees or transition problems. A listing label does not prove that STR use is legal, the bookings will continue, or its revenue will be yours after closing.',
 'Use the <a href="/blog/how-to-find-str-properties-for-sale/">STR property search guide</a> and the <a href="/markets/">local buying guides</a>. Keep a shortlist with listing links, asking price, jurisdiction, property type, estimated setup and missing evidence. Avoid spending the entire search period on a home that has not passed the basic gates.']),
('4. Build the property decision file before an offer',[
 ('table',['Question','Evidence to obtain','What remains uncertain'],[
 ['Can this address operate as intended?','Parcel jurisdiction, current permit path and association documents','Written permission, transfer conditions or unresolved restrictions'],
 ['What can it earn under my ownership?','Reconciled seller records and relevant comparable rentals','Availability, operating changes and seasonal downside'],
 ['What will ownership cost?','Taxes, STR insurance, management terms, utilities and repair bids','Reassessment, exclusions and expenses omitted from a projection'],
 ['Can I finance and insure this property?','Lender address review, appraisal conditions and an insurance quote','Approval conditions and costs before contingencies expire'],
 ['What am I buying besides the building?','Included inventory, contracts, deposits and proposed handoff','Items that do not transfer or need new agreements']]),
 'For financing that relies on property rent, ask what evidence the lender accepts. Fannie Mae’s <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b3-3.8-03/rental-income-subject-property-short-term-rental" rel="noopener">subject-property STR rental-income guidance</a> applies to eligible, legally permitted one-unit investment properties and specifies documentation. Seller forecasts and loan qualification are different checks.']),
('5. Convert the cash plan into a price decision',[
 'Illustrative first-buyer case: you allocate $150,000. A $400,000 purchase at an assumed 20% down uses $80,000 for the deposit. Add $12,000 closing costs, $25,000 setup, $10,000 repairs, a hypothetical $10,000 service fee and $20,000 retained reserves. The total is $157,000, creating a $7,000 gap. These are invented planning inputs, not a typical deal or a BNB service quote.',
 'With those non-deposit cash uses held fixed, the cash-only price ceiling is ($150,000 − $12,000 − $25,000 − $10,000 − $10,000 − $20,000) ÷ 0.20 = $365,000. This does not establish what the house is worth or what a lender will approve. Resolve the gap, negotiate a supportable price, change the scope, choose another property or pause. Do not double-count lender reserves as money available for furniture.',
 'Next, test owner cash flow with address-specific expenses and a downside revenue case. Use the <a href="/blog/compare-two-str-properties-before-offer/">property comparison framework</a> rather than buying the highest advertised gross revenue.']),
('6. Make an offer that preserves unresolved checks',[
 'Give your licensed buyer representative a clear maximum price and a list of conditions that still need verification. Ask the appropriate professionals to align inspection, financing, appraisal, insurance, permitted use and inventory questions with the contract deadlines. Track who must provide each document and when the purchase commitment changes.',
 'The offer memo should identify the evidence supporting the price, the cash required, the downside case and the conditions that would trigger a renegotiation or rejection. The <a href="/buy-a-short-term-rental/investment-memo-template/">investment memo worksheet</a> keeps that decision explicit.']),
('7. Verify the handoff before you treat the purchase as ready',[
 'An existing Airbnb is not automatically a transferable business. Confirm which furnishings, agreements, guest obligations and operating records are included, and what must be established in your own name. Agree with the relevant professionals on the lawful treatment of reservations, deposits, permits and access; do not assume a host account or rating history becomes yours.',
 'For a new setup, verify quotes, access, contractors, utilities, guest-safety work and the management agreement before choosing an opening target. Ownership and a guest-ready operation are separate milestones. Use the <a href="/buy-a-short-term-rental/launch-handoff-checklist/">launch handoff checklist</a>.']),
('8. Choose the work you want an acquisition team to coordinate',[
 'For a first STR, acquisition support can coordinate sourcing, analysis, transaction milestones and launch planning. You still provide the capital, approve material decisions and separately engage the professionals who perform their contracted work. Ask for deliverables, fees, exclusions and payment timing in writing.',
 'Review <a href="/done-for-you-airbnb/">help buying your first Airbnb</a>, <a href="/pricing/">pricing and the full purchase budget</a> and <a href="/case-studies/">property-specific client examples</a>. If you want to discuss a purchase now, bring available cash, financing status, preferred markets and one or two listing links to a <a href="/apply/">first-STR acquisition call</a>.']),
('Questions first-time STR buyers ask',[
 ('h3','How much money do I need to buy my first Airbnb?'),'There is no universal amount. Add the lender’s required down payment, actual closing costs, setup, repairs, quoted service fees and the cash you intend or are required to retain. Model the address and your financing rather than assuming that a generic percentage covers everything.',
 ('h3','Can BNB Accelerator help me find a first STR to buy?'),'Review the acquisition scope and current written proposal. BNB coordinates property sourcing and purchase work; the website is not a live listing feed and the client makes the purchase decision.',
 ('h3','Should my first STR be an existing Airbnb?'),'Compare legal use, seller evidence, included inventory, total cash, transition work and operating costs. An existing rental may simplify some work, but current bookings or advertised revenue do not prove the result under your ownership.',
 ('h3','How fast can I buy and open my first STR?'),'Set a target, then build a schedule from the contract, lender review, inspections, permitted use, property condition and vendors. No general timeline guarantees that a particular property will close or open by your desired date.']),
]
path='/blog/how-to-buy-first-airbnb/';title,desc,h1=CONFIG['blog/how-to-buy-first-airbnb/index.html'];trail=[('Home','/'),('Buying Guides','/blog/'),('Buying Your First Airbnb',path)]
body=f'''<section class="hero hero-page"><div class="wrap">{tpl.breadcrumb_html(trail)}<div class="hero-inner"><span class="eyebrow">First-property buying guide</span><h1>{h1}</h1><p>Published August 9, 2026 · Updated October 1, 2026</p></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap wrap-narrow"><article class="article"><p class="lead">Ready to buy your first short-term rental? Build a funded search, a property decision file and a clear offer ceiling. This walkthrough takes you from available capital to a purchase decision; use the <a href="/buy-a-short-term-rental/">buyer roadmap</a> to jump to the worksheet for your current stage.</p>{sections_html(sections)}<p>Primary source links checked October 1, 2026. Financing, local permission and costs must be verified for your own property and loan.</p></article></div></section>{tpl.cta_band('Bring your first-property plan to the call','Discuss your cash budget, financing status and candidate property before you commit.',('/apply/','Discuss My First STR'),('/tools/first-str-purchase-budget/','Build My Purchase Budget'))}'''
